  "narrative": "The pages used for phishing typically used obfuscated code to redirect the user to another webpage: In some pages the malicious redirect was disabled by the attackers, by placing additional JavaScript on the page which would redirect users to a legitimate site preferentially. Sample 5e3bea788e89e0814e898b4a648b93c0b74f7e2c Decoy documents are used in conjunction with malware droppers in order to make the target believe the file they have just opened is legitimate. For example the screenshot below shows the contents of a credential phishing website designed to mimic the legitimate OWA site of a defence contractor.",
